msgid "Instruction Execution & ALU"
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:291
msgid "ALU Operation & Register Access"
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:293
msgid ""
"In strict compliance with the **AVR® Instruction Set Manual (DS40002198A,"
" Section 4)**, the high-performance AVR Arithmetic Logic Unit (ALU) "
"operates in direct connection with all 32 general-purpose registers:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:295
msgid ""
"**Single-Cycle Operation**: Arithmetic and logical register-to-register "
"operations execute within a single instruction transition. In this cycle:"
" 1. Two operand registers are read from the Register File. 2. The "
"operation (Arithmetic, Logical, or Bit manipulation) is evaluated. 3. The"
" result is written back to the destination register :math:`Rd`. 4. The "
"Status Register (SREG) condition flags are updated according to exact "
"Boolean algebraic formulas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:300
msgid ""
"**ALU Functional Blocks**: * **Arithmetic**: Addition (``ADD``, ``ADC``, "
"``ADIW``), Subtraction (``SUB``, ``SUBI``, ``SBC``, ``SBCI``, ``SBIW``), "
"Comparison (``CP``, ``CPI``), Negation (``NEG``), Increment (``INC``), "
"Decrement (``DEC``), and Multiplication (``MUL``, ``MULS``, ``MULSU``). *"
" **Logical**: Bitwise AND (``AND``, ``ANDI``, ``TST``), OR (``OR``, "
"``ORI``), Exclusive-OR (``EOR``, ``CLR``), and One's Complement "
"(``COM``). * **Bit & Shift Functions**: Bit set/clear (``SBI``, ``CBI``),"
" Shifts (``LSL``, ``LSR``, ``ASR``), Rotates through carry (``ROL``, "
"``ROR``), and Nibble swap (``SWAP``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:306
msgid "Fetch-Decode-Execute Cycle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:308
msgid "Tiny8 executes programs through the classical CPU cycle:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:321
msgid "Instruction Format & Encoding"
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:323
msgid ""
"In physical AVR microcontrollers: * Most instructions are **16-bit "
"(1-word)** opcodes. * Direct memory instructions (``LDS``, ``STS``) and "
"long jumps/calls (``JMP``, ``CALL``) are **32-bit (2-word)** opcodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:327
msgid ""
"In Tiny8, the assembler validates operands according to AVR DS40002198A "
"constraints (e.g., verifying that ``LDI``, ``SUBI``, ``CPI`` only target "
"upper registers R16–R31, and that ``ADIW`` / ``SBIW`` target valid "
"pointer register pairs), then stores them as pre-decoded execution "
"tuples:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:340
msgid "Step Tracing & State Inspection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:342
msgid ""
"During each execution step, Tiny8 records changes to facilitate visual "
"debugging:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:344
msgid ""
"**Register Trace**: Tracks register writes as ``(step, register_index, "
"new_value)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:345
msgid "**Memory Trace**: Tracks SRAM writes as ``(step, address, new_value)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:346
msgid ""
"**Step Telemetry**: Records PC, SREG flags, cycle counts, and call stack "
"backtraces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:349
msgid "Hardware Realism & AVR Compliance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:351
msgid ""
"Tiny8 is strictly grounded in the **Microchip AVR® Instruction Set Manual"
" (DS40002198A)**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:353
msgid ""
"**Instruction Set Fidelity**: All 61 supported instructions strictly "
"follow official Microchip AVR definitions, operands, and SREG Boolean "
"formulas without non-standard instruction extensions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:354
msgid ""
"**Hardware MUL Compliance**: In accordance with AVR DS40002198A, ``MUL "
"Rd, Rr`` writes the 16-bit unsigned product strictly into the dedicated "
"register pair ``R1:R0`` (R0 = low byte, R1 = high byte)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:355
msgid ""
"**Software Division**: Conforming to physical AVR silicon, integer "
"division is performed via standard software routines (e.g., subtraction "
"loops or shift-and-subtract) rather than non-standard hardware "
"instructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:356
msgid ""
"**Execution & Memory Model**: Instructions execute in discrete single-"
"step transitions across a unified flat address space with memory-mapped "
"I/O (ports 0x00..0x3F including CRT matrix and keyboard buffer) for full "
"visibility and educational inspectability."
msgstr ""

